---
description: Performance and accessibility
alwaysApply: true
---

Lazy load heavy components.

Use semantic HTML.

Use one `h1` per route. Associate every label, description, and error with its
control; composite fields and OTP need an explicit accessible name.

Support keyboard navigation, visible focus, radio-group arrow keys, and sheet
focus trapping.

Default touch targets are ≥48px; documented dense desktop exceptions are ≥40px.
Operational copy is ≥12px. Meet WCAG AA in light and dark.

Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` in CSS and programmatic scrolling.

Every data route needs loading, empty, error, permission, and offline behavior.
Service-worker updates must not discard active form input.
Mobile pull-to-refresh (AppShell) refetches active queries; ignore it when a
sheet is open or a form field is focused.

Optimize for Lighthouse.
